.TH TAIL 1 "2026" "KERNEL32" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tail \- affiche la fin des fichiers / output the last part of files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tail
[-n [+]N] [-c [+]N] [-fqv] [file...]
.br
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints the last 10 lines of each file; works on pipes. +N starts at line N. -f keeps polling the files for appended data.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -n N
Last N lines.
.TP
.B -c N
Last N bytes.
.TP
.B -f
Follow appended data.
.SH SEE ALSO
head(1)
